From: conda-forge maintainers
Subject: cli: default to pysemgrep on non-unix

The default branch of main() execs osemgrep (semgrep-core via argv[0]).
For most commands osemgrep falls back to pysemgrep, and on non-unix that
fallback spawn exits 1 with no output. Run the Python CLI directly there,
as --legacy does.

--- a/cli/src/semgrep/console_scripts/entrypoint.py
+++ b/cli/src/semgrep/console_scripts/entrypoint.py
@@ -302,7 +302,11 @@
         # (and legacy is not specified)
         # and osemgrep needs to fallback on pysemgrep
         os.environ["SEMGREP_NEW_CLI_UX"] = f"{int(sys.stdout.isatty())}"
-        exec_osemgrep()
+        if IS_WINDOWS:
+            # non-unix: skip osemgrep, run the Python CLI directly
+            exec_pysemgrep()
+        else:
+            exec_osemgrep()


 if __name__ == "__main__":
